  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Teaching the Teachers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will address the need for locally trained female teachers and teaching assistants in Galgaduud region of Somalia, which until seven years ago had no tradition of education. Iftiin, the applicant, has opened eight schools and runs four literacy campaigns, but the difficulties of recruiting and retaining teachers are immense. They tend to stay for only short periods, and are exclusively male. The five year project will provide teacher training through a two year certificate course given by a local university but school based. This will mean female student teachers can live at home, and are unlikely to leave the region. The impact will be long term and educationally significant.</narrative>
  </description>
